  "APIProfile":           "Basic",
  "Execution":            "Continuous",
  "Description":          "Voice Command Interface: a person talks to an application and the application answers aloud. The same for every application: the application is given to it as the schemas of its commands and of its responses (the DataXMData of the L3 of JSON Interface, MMC-JSI). Automatic Speech Recognition recognises the speech; JSON Interface turns what the person asked into a command, an Application JSON Instance (MMC-AJI) that conforms to the application's schema, and turns the application's response, also an Application JSON Instance, into facts; Entity Dialogue Processing, which holds the dialogue, says what is to be said - an answer, a question when the request is not clear, what was done or why not - from the recognised text and the facts; Text to Speech speaks it. The command goes out on a Port and the response comes in on a Port, whatever the application. The speech that carries commands is not the speech an application edits: they arrive on different Ports. A response is said when it arrives: the application may take time.",

  "InternalTypes":        [],

